	(text "MK20DX128VFM5 running DAPLink (k20dx HIC), powered from +5V through its own USB regulator (VOUT33 -> VDD)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16 19.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b69bdd24-79e0-5d35-b245-5d324967ca4c")
	)
	(text "Pin use follows the DAPLink k20dx HIC: PTC5 = SWCLK, PTC6 = SWDIO, PTB1 = nRESET to the K64, PTD4 = LED,"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16 22.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b81220d0-a96d-5bf0-b7a5-c783513559a3")
	)
	(text "UART1 PTC3/PTC4 bridges to the K64 UART0 (CDC console). Pins verified against DAPLink k20dx IO_Config.h and the FRDM-K64F OpenSDA circuit:"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16 25.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "95594a90-b68c-5d04-aed9-3a0af76310e9")
	)
	(text "PTC7 (SWDIO_IN) ties to SWDIO, 33 R in series with USB D+/D- (FRDM R20/R22). No level shifters: the K64 target is 3.3 V like the K20."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16 27.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "17a70224-00c0-54eb-b536-62f253a76302")
	)
	(text "J601 programs the K20 itself (bootloader + DAPLink). SW601 held at power-up enters DAPLink maintenance mode."
